<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-13296] .NET: TransactionImpl finalizer can crash the process</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-13296</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;~TransactionImpl potentially throws an exception (e.g. when grid is stopped), causing the entire process to abort.&lt;br/&gt;
GetLocalActiveTransactions is especially problematic - the method is informational, yet will result in all the returned transactions to be finalized later.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Finalizers should not throw exceptions&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Stopped grid is a valid use case&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;GetLocalActiveTransactions should be fixed to return &quot;read-only&quot; transactions that won&apos;t be finalized&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Review all filalizers and make sure they are safe.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
